# Normalize line endings for all text files: store as LF in the repo,
# check out using the platform's native convention. This is the baseline
# fix for issue #159 (mixed CRLF/LF files with no normalization policy
# caused an editor touch to flip an entire file and bury the real diff).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must run on Linux containers/CI regardless of the
# committer's platform — force LF unconditionally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Visual Studio solution files are conventionally CRLF and Visual Studio
# itself rewrites them that way on save; forcing LF here would just cause
# perpetual churn against that tooling. Keep the existing CRLF convention.
*.sln text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never subject to text normalization or diffing as text.
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
